  "issue": "M60 clojure deep round — CLJ-D19 (declaration gate) + CLJ-D27 (type privacy)",
  "note": "A protocol/interface signature and a method IMPLEMENTATION are DECLARATIONS, and no core-builtin gate belongs on them. The gate that dropped them was a leftover from C9, whose real fix was the null-prototype alias table — `toString` was never in the core list, so the gate never fired for the prototype-pollution class it was written for. What it did instead was delete real members: gvec.clj's `(definterface ArrayManager …)` declared `array`, `alength`, `aclone`, `aget`, `aset` and four of the five are core names, so the interface shipped with ONE method; `(definterface … (identity [x]))` shipped with none. The shapes below are the gvec/genclass shapes exactly, plus `get`/`key`/`count`, which the 723-name list would have swallowed as well. CLJ-D27 rides along: `^:private` on a defprotocol/defrecord/deftype name is the same privacy contract W24-mr3 established for def/defn, and the type branches never read it.",
